WEBVTT

00:00:04.987 --> 00:00:07.307
-Here I come, boy!
-TACO: No, no, no!

00:00:07.547 --> 00:00:08.907
(GROANING)

00:00:12.347 --> 00:00:13.107
Oh, no.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.347
Buckle up, everybody!

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:18.227
It's Fritter time!

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.307
(CROWD CHEERING)

00:00:19.907 --> 00:00:22.667
CROWD: (CHANTING) Fritter! Fritter!

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.707
Fritter! Fritter! Fritter!

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:27.067
We love you, Miss Fritter.

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:33.467
Oh, yeah! Your license plate's gonna
look real nice in my collection.

00:00:34.107 --> 00:00:35.507
-Oh, boy.
-Run!

00:00:36.827 --> 00:00:37.947
Oh, no.

00:00:38.387 --> 00:00:41.027
Remember, obey all
appropriate street signs.

00:00:41.267 --> 00:00:42.627
-Cruz!
-(LAUGHS)

00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:48.987
-(MUD SQUELCHING)
-(GRUNTING)

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.627
Whoa! Hey--

00:00:50.747 --> 00:00:52.627
Whoa, whoa, whoa. (GRUNTS)

00:00:53.187 --> 00:00:56.747
-Oh, my gracious! Miss Fritter's down!
-(ALL GASPING)

00:00:57.987 --> 00:00:59.427
(GRUNTING)

00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:00.987
(REVVING)

00:01:01.707 --> 00:01:03.027
(CLATTERING)

00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:04.867
MISS FRITTER: Nobody touches him.

00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:07.067
He is mine! (GRUNTS)

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:10.987
You gonna get it now, Whipplefilter!

00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:13.267
(GRUNTING)

00:01:13.307 --> 00:01:16.107
Come on, McQueen. You can do it.
Come on, Lightning, keep going.

00:01:17.227 --> 00:01:19.027
ANNOUNCER: Miss Fritter is
looking to get upright, folks.

00:01:19.587 --> 00:01:20.787
And she is not pleased.

00:01:21.427 --> 00:01:23.667
CAR: Get up. Get up!
CROWD: Fritter! Fritter!

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:27.347
You about to feel the wrath of the...

00:01:27.547 --> 00:01:30.147
Lower Belleville County
Unified School District!

00:01:35.507 --> 00:01:37.027
Oh! What the-- Wait--

00:01:37.187 --> 00:01:38.307
(SCREAMING)

00:01:39.027 --> 00:01:40.547
No, no, no! No! No!

00:01:41.547 --> 00:01:42.667
(GASPS)

00:01:43.427 --> 00:01:45.707
ANNOUNCER: Ladies and gentlemen,
we have a winner!

00:01:45.787 --> 00:01:47.547
Frances Beltline!

00:01:47.627 --> 00:01:51.027
Is that me? That's me! I won! I won!

00:01:51.107 --> 00:01:54.187
-Cruz! Cruz! No!
-Ahhh! Watch out!

00:01:55.707 --> 00:01:58.627
Whoa, whoa. (WHIMPERS)

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.187
(WATER GUSHING)

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.467
-(CROWD GASPS)
-(SPITS)

00:02:12.507 --> 00:02:14.027
MALE CAR: Whipplefilter?

00:02:19.387 --> 00:02:21.707
-It's Lightning McQueen!
-(ALL SCREAMING)

00:02:22.147 --> 00:02:23.187
(GASPS)

00:02:23.507 --> 00:02:25.067
-CAR: McQueen!
-(CAMERAS FLASHING)

00:02:25.747 --> 00:02:27.467
(HORN BLARING)

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.587
Fans here at Thunder Hollow
still buzzing over tonight's...

00:02:30.747 --> 00:02:32.907
unexpected appearance
of Lightning McQueen.

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:34.667
He has always been my favorite!

00:02:34.827 --> 00:02:37.947
My garage is covered from
head to toe with 95 posters.

00:02:38.107 --> 00:02:40.387
REPORTER: Tell our listeners at home
you weren't really trying

00:02:40.467 --> 00:02:42.027
-to wreck him, were you?
-So trophy's kind of nice.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.227
Don't you think?

00:02:44.747 --> 00:02:48.107
I mean, I know you got like
a billion of them, so you would know.

00:02:50.427 --> 00:02:52.587
I still can't believe I won. (CHUCKLES)

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:54.747
It's pretty shiny.
I have never seen one up close.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.027
Looks like they spent
a lot of money on it.

00:02:57.107 --> 00:02:58.467
I mean, I think it's real metal.

00:02:58.627 --> 00:03:01.267
Stop. Just stop, okay, Cruz?
You don't even know.

00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:04.507
-You don't even have one clue--
-Hey! I was just trying--

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:07.067
Do you know what happens
if I lose this race?

00:03:08.427 --> 00:03:12.427
Every mile of this trip was to get me
faster than Jackson Storm. Faster!

00:03:13.107 --> 00:03:15.747
I started off getting nowhere
for a week on a simulator!

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:18.107
I lose a whole day with you
on Fireball Beach.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:21.627
And then I waste tonight
in the crosshairs of Miss Fritter!

00:03:21.947 --> 00:03:24.387
I'm stuck in the same speed
I was a month ago!

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:28.747
I can't get any faster because
I'm too busy taking care of my trainer!

00:03:30.147 --> 00:03:34.467
This is my last chance, Cruz.
Last! Final! Finito!

00:03:34.627 --> 00:03:37.467
If I lose, I never get to do this again.

00:03:37.507 --> 00:03:38.987
If you were a racer...

00:03:39.147 --> 00:03:43.307
you'd know what I'm talking about
but you're not! So you don't.

00:03:44.507 --> 00:03:45.707
(CRUZ GASPS)

00:03:49.307 --> 00:03:50.747
Mack! Pull over!

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:52.347
What? Now?

00:03:52.587 --> 00:03:53.787
Now!

00:03:54.627 --> 00:03:56.267
Ahh! Okay! Pulling over!

00:04:02.347 --> 00:04:05.147
Ask me if I dreamed of being a trainer,
Mr. McQueen. Go ahead.

00:04:06.507 --> 00:04:09.427
Ask me if I got up in the dark

00:04:09.587 --> 00:04:11.547
to run laps before school every day.

00:04:11.707 --> 00:04:14.867
Ask me if I saved every penny
to buy a ticket

00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:16.747
to the races when they came to town.

00:04:16.827 --> 00:04:21.027
Ask me if I did that so I could be
a trainer someday. Ask me.

00:04:22.187 --> 00:04:23.667
-Did you?
-No!

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:26.907
I've wanted to become a racer forever!

00:04:28.027 --> 00:04:29.267
Because of you!

00:04:34.867 --> 00:04:38.267
I used to watch you on TV,
flying through the air.

00:04:39.627 --> 00:04:43.067
You seemed so... fearless.

00:04:46.427 --> 00:04:50.027
"Dream small, Cruz,"
that's what my family used to say.

00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:52.787
"Dream small or not at all."

00:04:55.547 --> 00:04:57.227
They were just trying to protect me.

00:04:58.547 --> 00:05:01.147
But I was the fastest kid in town

00:05:01.227 --> 00:05:03.507
and I was gonna prove them wrong.

00:05:05.507 --> 00:05:06.907
What happened?

00:05:08.227 --> 00:05:11.867
When I got to my first race,
I figured it out.

00:05:13.187 --> 00:05:14.307
What?

00:05:16.987 --> 00:05:18.627
That I didn't belong.

00:05:19.547 --> 00:05:21.507
The other racers looked nothing like me.

00:05:23.267 --> 00:05:28.467
They were bigger and stronger
and so... confident.

00:05:30.827 --> 00:05:35.067
And when they started their engines,
that was it...

00:05:35.227 --> 00:05:37.547
I knew I'd never be a racer.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.347
I just left.

00:05:43.947 --> 00:05:47.107
It was my one shot and I didn't take it.

